I, myself, find tourists rather hard and monks easy.  Hmmmm...which
makes me wonder: maybe I should start giving an honest effort at other
classes (if monks really _are_ hard)?

Monks are easier in the beginning stages.  The deal a decent amount of
damage, and, as you stated, gain intrinsics. The amount of damage
dealt becomes less significant in the latter stages - you are limited
by bare-handed alone.  I usually gain 'Grand Master' way before the
mid-part of the game.  Of course, you can use weapons, but are limited
on advancement of skill slots.  I find weapon-using monks to be an
arduous task.

Key intrinsics, that are more crucial in the latter game, are
difficult to attain (if at all), without consuming flesh.

Armor can also become an issue.  You cannot wear any body armor except
for a robe.  Anything else greatly hampers fighting ability.
Therefore, any DSM is out of the question.

But, these are only a few examples of why monks can be hard (without
going into detail)...

